# IMPORTANT PROJECT PRINCIPLES

1. Do not generate questions from the resume alone.
   Use structured entities + relationships + retrieved resume context.

2. Do not assume relationship extraction is perfect.
   Measure its accuracy during Phase 9.

3. Do not assume questions are hallucination-free.
   Validate every generated question against available resume evidence.

4. Do not make the interview static.
   The next question should depend on the candidate's previous answer.

5. Do not rely only on an overall score.
   Track specific strengths, weaknesses, claims, relationships,
   and knowledge gaps.

6. Do not build unnecessary features during the MVP.
   Focus on the core intelligence pipeline.

7. Keep PostgreSQL responsible for structured application data.
   Use the retrieval/vector layer only where semantic retrieval
   actually provides value.

8. Keep the system modular so individual AI components can be
   replaced or improved without rewriting the entire application.

